<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
  <meta name="color-scheme" content="dark">
  <title>Child Safety Standards - Pressboxd</title>

  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/static/styles.css">

  <style>
    html, body, body.app { background:#000; }

    .policyPage {
      width:min(100%,860px);
      margin:0 auto;
      padding:26px 18px 48px;
    }

    .policyHeader {
      padding:12px 0 22px;
      border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.12);
      margin-bottom:24px;
    }

    .policyLogo {
      display:inline-block;
      text-decoration:none;
      margin-bottom:18px;
    }

    .policyLogo img {
      display:block;
      width:auto;
      height:42px;
      max-width:220px;
      object-fit:contain;
    }

    .policyHeader h1 {
      margin:0;
      font-size:clamp(28px,5vw,42px);
      line-height:1.05;
      letter-spacing:-.03em;
    }

    .policyEffective {
      margin-top:8px;
      color:var(--muted,#a3adbb);
      font-size:13px;
    }

    .policyIntro {
      margin:0 0 26px;
      font-size:15px;
      line-height:1.65;
      color:rgba(255,255,255,.88);
    }

    .policySection {
      padding:22px 0;
      border-top:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.09);
    }

    .policySection:first-of-type {
      border-top:0;
      padding-top:0;
    }

    .policySection h2 {
      margin:0 0 12px;
      font-size:19px;
      line-height:1.2;
    }

    .policySection p,
    .policySection li {
      color:rgba(255,255,255,.82);
      font-size:14px;
      line-height:1.65;
    }

    .policySection p { margin:10px 0 0; }

    .policySection ul {
      margin:10px 0 0;
      padding-left:22px;
    }

    .policySection li + li { margin-top:5px; }

    .policySection strong { color:#fff; }

    .policyContact {
      border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.14);
      background:#0b0b0b;
      padding:14px;
      margin-top:14px;
      border-radius:0;
    }

    .policyContact a {
      color:var(--accent,#6ea6ff);
      overflow-wrap:anywhere;
    }

    .policyBack {
      display:inline-flex;
      align-items:center;
      min-height:36px;
      padding:7px 10px;
      margin-top:24px;
      border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.16);
      border-radius:0;
      color:#fff;
      text-decoration:none;
      background:transparent;
      font-size:13px;
      font-weight:700;
    }

    .policyBack:hover { background:rgba(255,255,255,.06); }

    @media (max-width:600px) {
      .policyPage { padding:18px 12px 80px; }
      .policyLogo img { height:32px; }
      .policyHeader { margin-bottom:18px; padding-bottom:17px; }
      .policySection { padding:17px 0; }
      .policySection p, .policySection li { font-size:13px; }
    }
  </style>
</head>

<body class="app">
  <main class="policyPage">
    <header class="policyHeader">
      <a class="policyLogo" href="/shows" aria-label="Pressboxd">
        <img src="/static/pressboxd-wordmark.png" alt="Pressboxd">
      </a>

      <h1>Child Safety Standards</h1>
      <div class="policyEffective">Effective date: August 31, 2026</div>
    </header>

    <p class="policyIntro">
      Pressboxd is committed to maintaining a safe community and has zero
      tolerance for child sexual abuse and exploitation (CSAE) or child sexual
      abuse material (CSAM). These standards apply to all users and all
      community features available through the Pressboxd website and mobile app.
    </p>

    <section class="policySection">
      <h2>1. Prohibited Content and Conduct</h2>

      <p>Pressboxd strictly prohibits any content or behavior that sexually exploits, abuses, or endangers a child. This includes, but is not limited to:</p>

      <ul>
        <li>Creating, uploading, sharing, requesting, distributing, or promoting CSAM.</li>
        <li>Sexualizing or exploiting minors in images, videos, text, links, or other content.</li>
        <li>Grooming or attempting to groom a child for sexual purposes.</li>
        <li>Sextortion or threats involving sexual content concerning a minor.</li>
        <li>Soliciting sexual images, sexual activity, or sexual contact from a minor.</li>
        <li>Facilitating or promoting child trafficking or sexual exploitation.</li>
        <li>Using Pressboxd to direct users to external locations where CSAE or CSAM is available.</li>
        <li>Any other conduct that sexually exploits, abuses, or endangers a child.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="policySection">
      <h2>2. Reporting Child Safety Concerns</h2>

      <p>
        Users are encouraged to report any content or behavior that may involve
        CSAE, CSAM, grooming, exploitation, or another child-safety concern.
        Reports may be submitted through Pressboxd's in-app reporting or
        feedback features where available, or by contacting the child-safety
        email address below.
      </p>

      <div class="policyContact">
        <strong>Child Safety Contact:</strong><br>
        <a href="mailto:YOUR_CHILD_SAFETY_EMAIL">YOUR_CHILD_SAFETY_EMAIL</a>
      </div>

      <p>
        If a child is in immediate danger, contact local law enforcement or the
        appropriate emergency service in your region.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="policySection">
      <h2>3. Review and Enforcement</h2>

      <p>
        Pressboxd reviews credible reports of suspected CSAE or CSAM and takes
        appropriate action when violations are identified. Enforcement may
        include removal of content, restriction or termination of accounts,
        preservation of relevant information when legally appropriate, and
        referral to appropriate authorities.
      </p>

      <p>
        Accounts used to create, distribute, request, promote, or facilitate
        CSAE or CSAM may be permanently removed from Pressboxd.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="policySection">
      <h2>4. Handling CSAM</h2>

      <p>
        Pressboxd does not permit CSAM on its services. When Pressboxd obtains
        actual knowledge of apparent CSAM, we take appropriate steps to remove
        or restrict access to the material and take action against involved
        accounts in accordance with these standards and applicable law.
      </p>

      <p>
        Where required by applicable law, Pressboxd will report confirmed or
        apparent CSAM to the National Center for Missing & Exploited Children
        (NCMEC) or the appropriate regional authority and cooperate with lawful
        requests from law enforcement.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="policySection">
      <h2>5. Compliance With Child Safety Laws</h2>

      <p>
        Pressboxd seeks to comply with applicable child-safety laws and
        regulations in the jurisdictions in which it operates. We may preserve
        or disclose information when required by law or when reasonably
        necessary to protect a child from abuse or exploitation.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="policySection">
      <h2>6. Child Safety Point of Contact</h2>

      <p>
        Google Play, law enforcement, child-safety organizations, and users may
        contact Pressboxd regarding child-safety matters using the designated
        contact below.
      </p>

      <div class="policyContact">
        <strong>Pressboxd Child Safety Contact</strong><br>
        Email: <a href="mailto:YOUR_CHILD_SAFETY_EMAIL">YOUR_CHILD_SAFETY_EMAIL</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="policySection">
      <h2>7. Updates to These Standards</h2>

      <p>
        Pressboxd may update these Child Safety Standards as our service,
        enforcement practices, or legal obligations change. The effective date
        at the top of this page will be updated when these standards are revised.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="policySection">
      <h2>8. Related Policies</h2>

      <p>
        For additional information about how Pressboxd handles user information,
        please review our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>

      <a class="policyBack" href="/shows">Back to Pressboxd</a>
    </section>
  </main>
</body>
</html>
